# A part that ENFORCES 4.5.2's "at most one bit is 1b" instead of tolerating a
# violation: a software write asserting MNG or HW latches, and while latched SW
# ownership is never granted. Off by default and it must stay that way -- whether
# the real PCH enforces this is the campaign's open proposition, not a fact.
#
# The release is what makes the arm non-vacuous, and that was MEASURED. With MNG
# never held the register starts at zero, so a read-modify-writing driver reads
# zero and the defect cannot appear. With MNG held forever no acquire can succeed
# however correct the protocol is. Only a firmware release separates the two.
-i219-extcnf-strict -i219-mng-release-after 3